   "note": "Load holding fails during a slow leak at 20 degrees, so the walker is lost either way; the models differ in which actuator gives out first. Level 1 ties leg force and centre-of-pressure authority to the same capacity (A3, A4) and tips. Level 2 tips with ankle 20 and knee 60 kN m, holds through the run with ankle 26.5 and knee 60 kN m, and drops the cockpit at 2.8 m/s with the adopted torques (ankle 40.5, knee 26.5 kN m, DQ-024): weaker knees turn the tip into a drop (HAZ-PIL-002)."
